  "review": [
    "Read every one of 33 route diffs. Changes preserve typed error dispatch, status/code/message/preview responses, cache headers, all request/auth/service/write ordering and existing Today bounds log suppression. Only logger import/call and now-unused catch binding differ.",
    "Read seven HRM wrapper catch diffs and actual wrapper tests. Existing return versus await semantics unchanged; async downstream rejection remains downstream rejection rather than new auth503 remapping.",
    "Read helper literal union and unchanged fixed sinks; no thrown object, name, message, stack, cause, case/employee/location identifier added to the new call inputs.",
    "Read 46-row fixture catalog and actual imported-route privacy test implementation. Four synthetic thrown variants reach each selected fault target exactly once, with actual logger assertion. Auth, validation, service and Prisma dependencies are mocked; these are not live authorization, persistence or full handler happy-path tests.",
    "Read 18 typed-response tests and both preserved bulk409 preview cases. They sample domain branches, not every possible domain code.",
    "Read telemetry test implementation: finite output keys/categories and 500 invalid input tuples are synthetic console-level checks; no live provider ingestion or destination was tested.",
    "Read corrected source scanner and existing evidenceAccessSnapshot implementation. One private forwarding adapter has precisely two current literal operation callers; scanner now explicitly checks declaration and references rather than exempting the entire file.",
    "Reviewed exact three Play Integrity constant substitutions and independently ran existing behavioral tests; no policy or verdict decision branch changed."
